    "result_text": "The test passes, but most of this was already built before I changed anything. The app already supported a percentage or a flat amount discount, took it off before tax, showed it on the invoice, and had a percentage/amount choice in the discount form. `bin/e2e` passed on the untouched code.\n\nWhat was missing was \"either/or\": the server would accept a percentage and a flat amount on the same invoice and stack them. I closed that gap at each layer:\n\n- **Database** (`V44__discount_one_kind.sql`): a new check constraint means an invoice can't hold both kinds. Any existing invoice that has both is first converted to a single flat amount equal to what the two took off together, so its total doesn't change.\n  - The app's database is in-memory and starts empty, so this conversion never ran against real rows. The logic is untested on data.\n- **Server**: the discount request now fails validation with a 400 if both are non-zero, and the invoice itself refuses to store both. Checked by hand: sending both gets 400; a flat amount alone or a percentage alone gets 200.\n- **Front end**: the invoice no longer has the combined \"$X off plus Y%\" wording. It shows either \"Discount (Y%)\" or \"Discount ($X off)\" next to the amount taken off. Every existing `data-testid` is kept.\n\nOne thing to be aware of: the test seed endpoint now fails loudly if a fixture gives both `discountPct` and `discountAmount`. Older discount specs that combined them would need updating, though the spec's own comment says updated copies of those specs exist elsewhere.\n\n`bin/e2e` passes: 1 of 1.",
